#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186373993 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129264 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f7a75441-d233-5a64-8d87-b3138c2d31be" :knowledge-point/title "Rewriting a Triple Integral Defined Over a Sphere"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f584638d-028d-5971-ba0e-0417d5a82f56" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{4}{\\rho }^{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta {sin}^{2}⁡ϕ\\,d\\rho \\,d\\theta \\,dϕ" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373995} {:answer/id #uuid "2d857b07-1c42-58b8-8329-7eaa3186040c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{16}{\\rho }^{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta {sin}^{2}⁡ϕ\\,d\\rho \\,d\\theta \\,dϕ" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373996} {:answer/id #uuid "e04bc74b-d742-5cfa-9631-89dd7639b707" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{4}{\\rho }^{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\\,d\\rho \\,d\\theta \\,dϕ" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373997} {:answer/id #uuid "5f381c92-b45b-5b5c-a647-e9da1acc98ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{16}{\\rho }^{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\\,d\\rho \\,d\\theta \\,dϕ" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373998} {:answer/id #uuid "e07ee0f1-8026-5d30-b8f1-6d1eaac9d4c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{4}{\\rho }^{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta {sin}^{2}⁡ϕ\\,d\\rho \\,d\\theta \\,dϕ" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373999}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f584638d-028d-5971-ba0e-0417d5a82f56" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{4}{\\rho }^{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta {sin}^{2}⁡ϕ\\,d\\rho \\,d\\theta \\,dϕ" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373995} :answer-field/id #uuid "a700385c-d096-5782-9773-03ac3b36124f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373994}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "52a77714-a767-5195-b412-fb970a316089" :question/math-academy-id "q-161747" :question/problem "The region $R$ is enclosed inside the sphere ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}=16.$\nExpress the following triple integral in spherical polar coordinates. \n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}y\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}V\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the change of variables formula in the form\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\,dV={∭}_{Δ}\\,f(\\rho \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\\rho \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\\rho \\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ)\\,{\\rho }^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\\,d\\rho \\,d\\theta \\,dϕ.\n$$\n\nIf $(\\rho ,\\theta ,ϕ)$ are the spherical coordinates of a point, then its Cartesian coordinates $(x,y,z)$ can be found by using the following formulas:\n\n$$\nx=\\rho \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\\,y=\\rho \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\\,z=\\rho \\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ\n$$\n\nNotice that the region $R$ represents the sphere of radius $4$ centered at the origin. \nAs a result, in spherical polar coordinates, our region can be expressed as \n\n$$\nΔ={(\\rho ,\\theta ,ϕ)\\,:\\,0\\le \\rho \\le 4,\\,0\\le \\theta \\le 2\\pi ,\\,0\\le ϕ\\le \\pi }.\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the spherical polar coordinates into the function $f(x,y,z)=y\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y,z) & =f(\\rho \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\\rho \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\\rho \\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ) \\\\  & =\\rho \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\\cdot \\rho  \\\\  & ={\\rho }^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the change of variables formula, we obtain  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∭}_{R}y\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}V & ={∭}_{Δ}{\\rho }^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\\cdot {\\rho }^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\\,d\\rho \\,d\\theta \\,dϕ \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{4}{\\rho }^{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta {sin}^{2}⁡ϕ\\,d\\rho \\,d\\theta \\,dϕ.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186374013 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129264 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f7a75441-d233-5a64-8d87-b3138c2d31be" :knowledge-point/title "Rewriting a Triple Integral Defined Over a Sphere"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ee3b2ce0-5cd4-5791-878f-f8f82186b93c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{1/9}{\\rho }^{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta {sin}^{2}⁡ϕ\\,d\\rho \\,d\\theta \\,dϕ" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374015} {:answer/id #uuid "68878230-bc31-5e28-8e1b-b63f15763b45" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\rho }^{2}{sin}^{2}⁡ϕ{cos}^{2}⁡ϕ\\,d\\rho \\,d\\theta \\,dϕ" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374016} {:answer/id #uuid "907334ea-42f3-5c05-8d16-981904231266" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{1/3}{\\rho }^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ\\,d\\rho \\,d\\theta \\,dϕ" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374017} {:answer/id #uuid "63e9f1ac-e3d1-5455-907a-07e8b2e69cd8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{1/9}{\\rho }^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ\\,d\\rho \\,d\\theta \\,dϕ" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374018} {:answer/id #uuid "ca042d11-6a9d-5f36-a85b-04076cae011f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{1/3}{\\rho }^{3}{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta {sin}^{2}⁡ϕ\\,d\\rho \\,d\\theta \\,dϕ" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374019}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "907334ea-42f3-5c05-8d16-981904231266" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{1/3}{\\rho }^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ\\,d\\rho \\,d\\theta \\,dϕ" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374017} :answer-field/id #uuid "0859bebc-de49-5160-95c6-b86c4e01bde8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374014}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "351698ef-ed69-59a8-a86e-a782ca5a2c9b" :question/math-academy-id "q-161756" :question/problem "The region $R$ is enclosed inside the sphere ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}=\\frac{1}{9}.$\nExpress the following triple integral in spherical polar coordinates. \n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}\\frac{yz}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}V\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the change of variables formula in the form\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\,dV={∭}_{Δ}\\,f(\\rho \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\\rho \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\\rho \\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ)\\,{\\rho }^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\\,d\\rho \\,d\\theta \\,dϕ.\n$$\n\nIf $(\\rho ,\\theta ,ϕ)$ are the spherical coordinates of a point, then its Cartesian coordinates $(x,y,z)$ can be found by using the following formulas:\n\n$$\nx=\\rho \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\\,y=\\rho \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\\,z=\\rho \\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ\n$$\n\nNotice that the region $R$ represents the sphere of radius $\\frac{1}{3}$ centered at the origin. \nAs a result, in spherical polar coordinates, our region can be expressed as \n\n$$\nΔ={(\\rho ,\\theta ,ϕ)\\,:\\,0\\le \\rho \\le \\frac{1}{3},\\,0\\le \\theta \\le 2\\pi ,\\,0\\le ϕ\\le \\pi }.\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the spherical polar coordinates into the function $f(x,y,z)=\\frac{yz}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y,z) & =f(\\rho \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\\rho \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\\rho \\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\rho \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\\cdot \\rho \\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ}{{(\\rho \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ)}^{2}+{(\\rho \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{\\rho }^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ}{{\\rho }^{2}{sin}^{2}⁡ϕ({cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta )} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the change of variables formula, we obtain  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∭}_{R}\\frac{yz}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}V & ={∭}_{Δ}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ}\\cdot {\\rho }^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\\,d\\rho \\,d\\theta \\,dϕ \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{1/3}{\\rho }^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ\\,d\\rho \\,d\\theta \\,dϕ.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186374020 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129281 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3d85b11c-498d-53b7-98f8-b742b46e8dc2" :knowledge-point/title "Rewriting a Triple Integral Defined Over a Part-Sphere"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "75e91f2c-ff7b-5513-b89a-4bcb03aa32fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{\\pi }^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}{\\rho }^{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ{sin}^{2}⁡ϕ\\,d\\rho \\,d\\theta \\,dϕ" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374022} {:answer/id #uuid "c3d6fcca-821b-55ff-9992-e519fbddcfbf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{3\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}{\\rho }^{2}{sin}^{2}⁡ϕ\\,d\\rho \\,d\\theta \\,dϕ" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374023} {:answer/id #uuid "8e29e753-a8bb-510f-a9fe-acdcacd87c97" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}{\\rho }^{2}{sin}^{2}⁡ϕ\\,d\\rho \\,d\\theta \\,dϕ" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374024} {:answer/id #uuid "9f637bb3-4d2f-502f-bf25-629597269741" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{\\pi }^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}{\\rho }^{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ\\,d\\rho \\,d\\theta \\,dϕ" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374025} {:answer/id #uuid "404a6135-3210-5e33-8138-c9310c8f40b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}{\\rho }^{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ{sin}^{2}⁡ϕ\\,d\\rho \\,d\\theta \\,dϕ" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374026}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "75e91f2c-ff7b-5513-b89a-4bcb03aa32fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{\\pi }^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}{\\rho }^{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ{sin}^{2}⁡ϕ\\,d\\rho \\,d\\theta \\,dϕ" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374022} :answer-field/id #uuid "42ef52b0-957a-5692-82da-972b7e58a760" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374021}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ac3d7303-e14a-5571-9831-0eb03f695bc9" :question/math-academy-id "q-161757" :question/problem "The region $R$ is enclosed inside the sphere ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}=2$ for $y\\le 0.$\nExpress the following triple integral in spherical polar coordinates. \n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}z\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}V\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the change of variables formula in the form\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\,dV={∭}_{Δ}\\,f(\\rho \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\\rho \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\\rho \\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ)\\,{\\rho }^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\\,d\\rho \\,d\\theta \\,dϕ.\n$$\n\nIf $(\\rho ,\\theta ,ϕ)$ are the spherical coordinates of a point, then its Cartesian coordinates $(x,y,z)$ can be found by using the following formulas:\n\n$$\nx=\\rho \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\\,y=\\rho \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\\,z=\\rho \\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ\n$$\n\nNotice that the region $R$ represents one-half of the sphere of radius $\\sqrt{2}$ centered at the origin.\n\n![](images/6f/6f35be4fd6773149597ea8a9dc8dd234e068da3f0fd3b2df32d11c61521bed75.png)\n\n \n\nAs a result, we obtain that in spherical polar coordinates, our region can be expressed as \n\n$$\nΔ={(\\rho ,\\theta ,ϕ)\\,:\\,0\\le \\rho \\le \\sqrt{2},\\,\\pi \\le \\theta \\le 2\\pi ,\\,0\\le ϕ\\le \\pi }.\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the spherical polar coordinates into the function $f(x,y,z)=z\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y,z) & =f(\\rho \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\\rho \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\\rho \\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ) \\\\  & =\\rho \\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ\\sqrt{(\\rho \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ)^{2}+(\\rho \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\rho \\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ\\sqrt{{\\rho }^{2}{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta {sin}^{2}⁡ϕ+{\\rho }^{2}{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta {sin}^{2}⁡ϕ} \\\\  & =\\rho \\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ\\sqrt{{\\rho }^{2}{sin}^{2}⁡ϕ({cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta )} \\\\  & =\\rho \\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ\\sqrt{{\\rho }^{2}{sin}^{2}⁡ϕ} \\\\  & ={\\rho }^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the change of variables formula, we obtain  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∭}_{R}z\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}V & ={∭}_{Δ}{\\rho }^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\\cdot {\\rho }^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\\,d\\rho \\,d\\theta \\,dϕ \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{\\pi }^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}{\\rho }^{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ{sin}^{2}⁡ϕ\\,d\\rho \\,d\\theta \\,dϕ.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186374027 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129281 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3d85b11c-498d-53b7-98f8-b742b46e8dc2" :knowledge-point/title "Rewriting a Triple Integral Defined Over a Part-Sphere"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d19066c6-b325-5560-9f52-0194219bafe2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{\\pi }^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{4}2{\\rho }^{4}{cos}^{2}⁡ϕ{sin}^{3}⁡ϕ\\,d\\rho \\,d\\theta \\,dϕ" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374029} {:answer/id #uuid "7ae1ba19-867d-5568-a509-341ceb448d77" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{\\pi }^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{4}2{\\rho }^{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta {sin}^{4}⁡ϕ\\,d\\rho \\,d\\theta \\,dϕ" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374030} {:answer/id #uuid "ce257804-eae4-5e24-957f-68bf333f63cc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{3\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{4}2{\\rho }^{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta {sin}^{4}⁡ϕ\\,d\\rho \\,d\\theta \\,dϕ" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374031} {:answer/id #uuid "b8d89c45-c854-5e9c-83b4-2db70cfab5ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{3\\pi /2}{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{4}2{\\rho }^{5}{sin}^{3}⁡ϕ\\,d\\rho \\,d\\theta \\,dϕ" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374032} {:answer/id #uuid "1b62ea51-2dba-54e7-a5f2-b1857169f664" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{3\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{4}2{\\rho }^{4}{sin}^{3}⁡ϕ\\,d\\rho \\,d\\theta \\,dϕ" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374033}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ce257804-eae4-5e24-957f-68bf333f63cc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{3\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{4}2{\\rho }^{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta {sin}^{4}⁡ϕ\\,d\\rho \\,d\\theta \\,dϕ" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374031} :answer-field/id #uuid "a7ce963d-75b4-566b-8c6b-5c5079626401" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374028}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "79d3cb68-3e16-5f1e-b189-33638dfa47d6" :question/math-academy-id "q-161760" :question/problem "The region $R$ is enclosed inside the sphere ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}=16$ for $x\\le 0.$\nExpress the following triple integral in spherical polar coordinates. \n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}2x({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}V\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the change of variables formula in the form\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\,dV={∭}_{Δ}\\,f(\\rho \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\\rho \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\\rho \\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ)\\,{\\rho }^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\\,d\\rho \\,d\\theta \\,dϕ.\n$$\n\nIf $(\\rho ,\\theta ,ϕ)$ are the spherical coordinates of a point, then its Cartesian coordinates $(x,y,z)$ can be found by using the following formulas:\n\n$$\nx=\\rho \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\\,y=\\rho \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\\,z=\\rho \\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ\n$$\n\nNotice that the region $R$ represents one-half of the sphere of radius $4$ centered at the origin.\n\n![](images/8c/8c803dbf5bcf6c2ece6c1c8352f96da1c88734ca1d792dd05593ac8c11527b2b.png)\n\n \n\nAs a result, we obtain that in spherical polar coordinates, our region can be expressed as \n\n$$\nΔ={(\\rho ,\\theta ,ϕ)\\,:\\,0\\le \\rho \\le 4,\\,\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\le \\theta \\le \\frac{3\\pi }{2},\\,0\\le ϕ\\le \\pi }.\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the spherical polar coordinates into the function $f(x,y,z)=2x({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y,z) & =f(\\rho \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\\rho \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\\rho \\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ) \\\\  & =2\\rho \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ((\\rho \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ)^{2}+(\\rho \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ)^{2}) \\\\  & =2\\rho \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ({\\rho }^{2}{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta {sin}^{2}⁡ϕ+{\\rho }^{2}{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta {sin}^{2}⁡ϕ) \\\\  & =2\\rho \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ({\\rho }^{2}{sin}^{2}⁡ϕ({cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta )) \\\\  & =2\\rho \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ({\\rho }^{2}{sin}^{2}⁡ϕ) \\\\  & =2{\\rho }^{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta {sin}^{3}⁡ϕ\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the change of variables formula, we obtain  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∭}_{R}2x({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}V & ={∭}_{Δ}2{\\rho }^{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta {sin}^{3}⁡ϕ\\cdot {\\rho }^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\\,d\\rho \\,d\\theta \\,dϕ \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{3\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{4}2{\\rho }^{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta {sin}^{4}⁡ϕ\\,d\\rho \\,d\\theta \\,dϕ.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186374034 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129264 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f7a75441-d233-5a64-8d87-b3138c2d31be" :knowledge-point/title "Rewriting a Triple Integral Defined Over a Sphere"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "539b8fda-c86f-55b0-9367-08e938349df7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{5}{\\rho }^{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta (\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ+1)\\,d\\rho \\,d\\theta \\,dϕ" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374036} {:answer/id #uuid "6a9eb0f4-a935-5119-a236-39dbba3ed79c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{5}}{\\rho }^{4}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ+\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )\\,d\\rho \\,d\\theta \\,dϕ" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374037} {:answer/id #uuid "8888c04e-b10c-5a7e-a43e-f3cb0618bec7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{5}}{\\rho }^{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ(\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ+\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ)\\,d\\rho \\,d\\theta \\,dϕ" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374038} {:answer/id #uuid "4f1bafdf-4325-57da-a5b4-8cca6ad7c0f7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{5}}{\\rho }^{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ({cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ)\\,d\\rho \\,d\\theta \\,dϕ" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374039} {:answer/id #uuid "bec6bbb8-1f99-5d2a-acfc-dbdcf7bd0cad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{5}{\\rho }^{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ(\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ+\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ)\\,d\\rho \\,d\\theta \\,dϕ" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374040}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8888c04e-b10c-5a7e-a43e-f3cb0618bec7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{5}}{\\rho }^{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ(\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ+\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ)\\,d\\rho \\,d\\theta \\,dϕ" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374038} :answer-field/id #uuid "33f7bfad-5a98-5c46-a455-8fe0419ad940" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374035}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "af7b91cf-b6cb-5d8f-879b-0e99c7144b05" :question/math-academy-id "q-161761" :question/problem "The region $R$ is enclosed inside the sphere ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}=5.$\nExpress the following triple integral in spherical polar coordinates. \n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}(x+z)\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}V\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the change of variables formula in the form\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\,dV={∭}_{Δ}\\,f(\\rho \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\\rho \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\\rho \\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ)\\,{\\rho }^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\\,d\\rho \\,d\\theta \\,dϕ.\n$$\n\nIf $(\\rho ,\\theta ,ϕ)$ are the spherical coordinates of a point, then its Cartesian coordinates $(x,y,z)$ can be found by using the following formulas:\n\n$$\nx=\\rho \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\\,y=\\rho \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\\,z=\\rho \\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ\n$$\n\nNotice that the region $R$ represents the sphere of radius $\\sqrt{5}$ centered at the origin. \nAs a result, in spherical polar coordinates, our region can be expressed as \n\n$$\nΔ={(\\rho ,\\theta ,ϕ)\\,:\\,0\\le \\rho \\le \\sqrt{5},\\,0\\le \\theta \\le 2\\pi ,\\,0\\le ϕ\\le \\pi }.\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the spherical polar coordinates into the function $f(x,y,z)=(x+z)\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y,z) & =f(\\rho \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\\rho \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\\rho \\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ) \\\\  & =(\\rho \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ+\\rho \\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ)\\cdot \\rho  \\\\  & ={\\rho }^{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ+\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the change of variables formula, we obtain  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∭}_{R}(x+z)\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}V & ={∭}_{Δ}{\\rho }^{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ+\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ)\\cdot {\\rho }^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\\,d\\rho \\,d\\theta \\,dϕ \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{5}}{\\rho }^{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ(\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ+\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ)\\,d\\rho \\,d\\theta \\,dϕ.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
